安珀·W. 写信给我们说，

23
00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:18.840
You mentioned doing a watch of Armageddon, and you guys will podcast the crap out of that.
你们提到要看《绝世天劫》，你们俩绝对会把这期播客做到极致。

24
00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:20.360
I need it in my life.
我的生活需要这个。

25
00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.260
And Kelly B.
还有来自印第安纳州韦斯特菲尔德的凯利·B.，

26
00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.300
from Westfield, Indiana, who listens with her family, said,
她和家人一起收听，她说道，

27
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:30.620
I've been listening to your podcast since the first episode, and it's truly my favorite one I listened to.
从第一期开始我就一直在听你们的播客，这真的是我听过最喜欢的播客。

28
00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.740
We desperately want you to break down Armageddon.
我们非常渴望你们能解析《绝世天劫》。

29
00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.400
You mentioned it, and we are all in.
你们提到了，我们全员奉陪。

30
00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.700
I showed it to my kids recently because you mentioned it, and it is so bad.
因为你们提到了，我最近把它放给我孩子们看了，这片子太烂了。

31
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.940
We totally need you to break it down.
我们绝对需要你们来解析它。

32
00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:44.720
Please, please.
求求你们了。

33
00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.160
Podcast the crap out of something might be my new favorite expression, Amber.
“把播客做到极致”可能会成为我最喜欢的新表达，安珀。

34
00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:55.920
You guys also know that this movie, Armageddon, does live in the lore of The Office.
大家也知道，这部电影《绝世天劫》确实存在于《办公室》的传说中。

35
00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:56.440
Yeah.
是的。

