00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:04.790
But I would listen to that DVD commentary again.
不过那个DVD随片讲评我倒是愿意再听一遍。

466
00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:06.410
I'm jealous you listened to it.
真嫉妒你听过了。

467
00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:10.810
I want to hear it because I'm going to play a little section of it later that I found.
我也想听，因为我待会儿会播放我找到的一小段。

468
00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:11.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

469
00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.390
And it really made me want to hear the whole thing.
这真的让我很想听完整版。

470
00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:15.310
I have six clips of it.
我截了六段音频。

471
00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:17.090
Great.
太棒了。

472
00:21:17.530 --> 00:21:21.530
And I will also share in stories for anyone who wants to listen to it.
我也会在故事里分享给任何想听的人。

473
00:21:21.530 --> 00:21:23.470
Well, listen, why don't we take a break?
好了，听着，我们为什么不休息一下？

474
00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:27.790
And then when we come back, we are going to break down Armageddon.
等我们回来后，就要好好剖析《世界末日》了。

475
00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:37.920
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请注意，所有WDNC的新老会员们。

476
00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:41.800
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这里是“我们毫不在乎俱乐部”播客。

477
00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:46.020
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年才发现，自己真的没那么多心思去在乎了。

478
00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:54.100
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在，我们要互相帮助，去搞懂潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、不靠谱的亲戚、脑雾和蝴蝶袖。

479
00:21:54.320 --> 00:21:56.960
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听到。

480
00:21:57.180 --> 00:21:58.860
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

481
00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:04.240
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcaSt.
在各大播客平台搜索并收听梅兰妮·桑德斯主持的“我们毫不在乎俱乐部”播客。

482
00:22:06.960 --> 00:22:08.320
All right, we're back.
好了，我们回来了。

483
00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:10.920
It's time to break down Armageddon.
是时候剖析《世界末日》了。

484
00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:14.200
This movie is going to open with a menacing voice.
这部电影开场会有一个低沉威胁的嗓音。

485
00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:16.420
Well, we open in outer space.
嗯，我们从外太空开始。

486
00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:16.840
Yeah.
对。

487
00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:18.440
We see the earth.
我们看到了地球。

488
00:22:18.780 --> 00:22:19.020
Yeah.
是啊。

489
00:22:19.180 --> 00:22:21.440
Something is hurtling toward it.
有什么东西正朝它飞驰而来。

490
00:22:21.800 --> 00:22:28.460
We find out that we're back in dinosaur times, and this meteor hit the earth back then.
我们发现时光倒流回了恐龙时代，这颗流星在那个时候撞击了地球。

491
00:22:28.640 --> 00:22:28.880
Yeah.
对。

492
00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:36.400
And you heard us earlier in this podcast recreate this opening narration that was originally done by Charlton Heston.
大家刚才在本期播客前面听到了我们重现这段原本由查尔顿·赫斯顿配音的开场旁白。

493
00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:37.280
That's right.
没错。

494
00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:41.120
One of my favorite things is the Chiron that comes up on the screen.
我最喜欢的一个细节就是屏幕上弹出的字幕条。

495
00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:46.040
I laughed out loud that it says 65 million years later.
看到上面写着“6500万年后”时我直接笑出声了。

496
00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:47.800
Well, here's the thing.
话虽如此。

497
00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:50.940
They have to do that for the 13-year-olds watching, right?
他们得为那些13岁的小观众这么做，对吧？

498
00:22:51.060 --> 00:22:53.900
It's like, cut to 65 million years later.
就像是，画面一转到了6500万年后。

499
00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:54.200
Yeah.
对。

500
00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:55.860
We're not in dinosaur times anymore.
我们不再处于恐龙时代了。

501
00:22:56.340 --> 00:23:00.860
I did love that when the letters of the movie come up, then they all blow apart.
我确实很喜欢电影片名字幕浮现然后全部炸碎的那个效果。

502
00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:05.720
Because everything in this movie is going to explode eventually, including the title of the movie.
因为这部电影里的所有东西最后都会爆炸，包括电影片名。

503
00:23:05.720 --> 00:23:08.900
And if you pay attention, it's right after they say a Michael Bay movie.
而且如果你注意看，就在他们说是迈克尔·贝电影之后。

504
00:23:09.060 --> 00:23:09.880
It explodes.
它就爆炸了。

505
00:23:10.220 --> 00:23:11.300
There's an immediate explosion.
立刻就发生了一场爆炸。

506
00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:11.720
It's perfect.
太完美了。

507
00:23:11.960 --> 00:23:13.300
We got this guy, Pete.
我们有这个叫皮特的家伙。

508
00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:14.440
He's an astronaut.
他是一名宇航员。

509
00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:16.300
He's outside of the spaceship.
他在宇宙飞船外面。

510
00:23:16.640 --> 00:23:19.080
He's tethered by one of those, like, cords.
他用那种类似于绳索的东西系着。

511
00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:19.720
Yeah.
对。

512
00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:21.680
He's fixing a satellite in space.
他正在太空中修理一颗卫星。

513
00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:22.060
Yeah.
对。

514
00:23:22.180 --> 00:23:22.960
That's what he's doing.
他就是在干这个。

515
00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:25.700
Billy Bob Thornton's back at mission control.
比利·鲍柏·松顿在地面指挥中心。

516
00:23:25.780 --> 00:23:30.740
And he's like, I'll give you a buffalo nickel if you just calm down a little bit.
他说，如果你能稍微冷静一点，我就送你一个水牛镍币。

517
00:23:30.860 --> 00:23:31.940
Can you do that for me?
你能为我做到这一点吗？

518
00:23:31.940 --> 00:23:33.920
His heart is racing in space.
他在太空中心跳加速。

519
00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.080
They're monitoring him.
他们在监测他的情况。

520
00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:35.300
Yeah.
对。

521
00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:35.580
Yeah.
对。

522
00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:38.160
And he's like, hey, buddy, we got plenty of time.
然后他说，嘿，老兄，我们有的是时间。

523
00:23:38.380 --> 00:23:40.080
So don't you worry.
所以你别担心。

524
00:23:40.300 --> 00:23:40.680
Oh.
哦。

525
00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:41.200
That's it.
就是这样。

526
00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:42.420
This guy's a goner.
这家伙死定惹。

527
00:23:42.880 --> 00:23:43.040
Yeah.
对。

528
00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:47.100
If someone says, don't you worry, you better get the hell out of there.
如果有人说别担心，你最好赶紧滚蛋。

529
00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:49.540
Did you notice Pete's blue eyes?
你注意到皮特那双蓝眼睛了吗？

530
00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:50.240
Yes.
注意到了。

531
00:23:50.480 --> 00:23:52.420
I was like, is this Josh Lucas?
我当时想，这是乔什·卢卡斯吗？

532
00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:54.360
Is this a young Josh Lucas?
这是一个年轻的乔什·卢卡斯吗？

533
00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:55.500
I thought the same thing.
我也这么想。

534
00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:56.760
I looked it up.
我查了一下。

535
00:23:56.900 --> 00:23:57.220
It's not.
不是。

536
00:23:57.220 --> 00:23:57.600
I did too.
我也查了。

537
00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:58.220
It's not.
不是。

538
00:23:58.400 --> 00:24:00.220
It's a stunt actor named Ian Quinn.
是一个叫伊恩·奎因的特约演员。

539
00:24:00.220 --> 00:24:02.840
And with the most beautiful blue eyes.
而且有着最美丽的蓝眼睛。

540
00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:03.340
Gorgeous.
美极了。

541
00:24:03.660 --> 00:24:04.020
Gorgeous.
美极了。

542
00:24:04.240 --> 00:24:07.040
He's going to get hit by something falling from the sky.
他会被从天而降的东西击中。

543
00:24:07.180 --> 00:24:08.420
They don't know what at firSt.
起初他们不知道是什么。

544
00:24:08.560 --> 00:24:11.180
But all this shit starts raining down.
但所有这些破烂开始像雨一样倾泻而下。

545
00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:13.080
We're 45 seconds into the movie.
电影才开始45秒。

546
00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:14.520
Things are already exploding.
东西就已经在爆炸了。

547
00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:16.240
The shuttle explodes.
航天飞机爆炸了。

548
00:24:16.460 --> 00:24:18.060
And then the satellite explodes.
然后卫星爆炸了。

549
00:24:18.200 --> 00:24:18.640
All of it.
全炸了。

550
00:24:18.700 --> 00:24:19.580
Pete explodes.
皮特也爆炸了。

551
00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:20.860
Down on Earth.
回到地球。

552
00:24:21.080 --> 00:24:23.000
The military thinks these are bogeys.
军方认为这些是敌机。

553
00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:24.300
They could be getting attacked.
他们可能正在遭受攻击。

554
00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:24.880
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

555
00:24:24.880 --> 00:24:25.640
I'm calling bullshit.
我觉得这是胡扯。

556
00:24:25.920 --> 00:24:27.360
We're getting attacked from space.
我们正在遭受来自太空的攻击。

557
00:24:27.540 --> 00:24:28.160
What's happening?
怎么回事？

558
00:24:28.280 --> 00:24:29.060
This is what they say.
他们是这么说的。

559
00:24:29.060 --> 00:24:30.300
They said, is it missiles?
他们问，是导弹吗？

560
00:24:30.540 --> 00:24:32.320
Is it an internal malfunction?
是内部故障吗？

561
00:24:32.660 --> 00:24:33.680
Is it a glitch?
是系统故障吗？

562
00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:34.940
Is it a wild card?
是突发状况吗？

563
00:24:35.180 --> 00:24:39.220
They create little pods of people for all of these different scenarios.
他们针对所有这些不同的假设情况，组建了不同的智囊小组。

564
00:24:39.440 --> 00:24:40.660
Figure out what it is.
弄清楚这到底是什么。

565
00:24:40.820 --> 00:24:45.400
I have a clip from the DVD commentary I want to play for you guys about this opening number.
我有一段DVD评论音轨想放给你们听，关于这段开场曲。

566
00:24:46.580 --> 00:24:47.520
Opening number.
开场曲。

567
00:24:48.040 --> 00:24:49.400
That's what you call it.
你是这么叫它的。

568
00:24:49.580 --> 00:24:50.320
Opening sequence.
开场序列。

569
00:24:50.580 --> 00:24:50.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

570
00:24:51.140 --> 00:24:51.300
Scene.
场景。

571
00:24:51.680 --> 00:24:55.320
Michael Bay said he hired a young writer to do a rewrite.
迈克尔·贝说他雇了一个年轻编剧来重写剧本。

572
00:24:55.560 --> 00:24:57.080
He doesn't say the name of the person.
他没有说出这人的名字。

573
00:24:57.080 --> 00:25:01.260
He says this young guy rewrote 53 pages in two days.
他说这个年轻人两天内重写了53页。

574
00:25:01.460 --> 00:25:03.520
And then Bay read the new script.
然后贝读了新剧本。

575
00:25:03.740 --> 00:25:07.040
And I quote, Michael Bay said, it was pure shit.
我引用一下，迈克尔·贝说，这纯粹是狗屎。

576
00:25:07.400 --> 00:25:09.400
He then gave the young writer this note.
然后他对年轻编剧提出了这样的意见。

577
00:25:09.620 --> 00:25:14.400
And I quote again, in the opening, you have to grab the audience by the balls.
我再引用一次，在开场，你必须一把揪住观众的睾丸。

578
00:25:14.740 --> 00:25:16.940
So this sent the writer back to work.
于是这让编剧回去重新干活。

579
00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:18.600
How do I grab him by the balls?
我怎么揪住他们的睾丸？

580
00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:19.860
And he came up with this.
然后他想出了这个。

581
00:25:20.040 --> 00:25:23.780
This idea that this whole thing goes kablooey right away.
这个想法就是整件事一上来就轰的一声炸上天。

582
00:25:23.780 --> 00:25:25.780
Well, now we're going to cut to Carl.
好了，现在我们要切到卡尔。

583
00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:27.200
He's a man.
他是个男人。

584
00:25:27.320 --> 00:25:30.440
He's sitting inside of, I don't know, a grain silo.
他坐在，我不知道，一个谷仓里。

585
00:25:30.560 --> 00:25:32.480
He's looking up at the sky with a telescope.
他正用望远镜抬头看着天空。

586
00:25:32.540 --> 00:25:34.180
He's got a homemade telescope, guys.
他有个自制的望远镜，伙计们。

587
00:25:34.400 --> 00:25:36.080
He was played by John Mahon.
他由约翰·马霍恩饰演。

588
00:25:36.360 --> 00:25:42.860
And his wife, Dottie, played by Grace Zabritsky, is going to throw the door open.
而他的妻子多蒂，由格蕾丝·扎布里茨基饰演，一把推开了门。

589
00:25:42.860 --> 00:25:45.980
And she's really mad because he hasn't come in for dinner.
她非常生气，因为他没有进屋吃晚饭。

590
00:25:46.300 --> 00:25:49.420
I mean, his Stouffer's Pot Pie sat on the table for 10 hours.
我是说，他的司特富烤鸡派在桌上放了10个小时。

591
00:25:49.520 --> 00:25:50.600
She wants a divorce.
她想要离婚。

592
00:25:51.000 --> 00:25:51.840
She's pissed.
她气炸了。

593
00:25:51.840 --> 00:25:55.700
This character of Dottie is going to set the tone for all women in this film.
多蒂这个角色将为这部电影里的所有女性定下基调。

594
00:25:55.900 --> 00:26:03.220
If you are a woman in this film, you are either a shrew wife, a stripper, a bitch with no sense of humor, or Liv Tyler.
如果你是这部电影里的女性，你要么是个唠叨的泼妇，要么是个脱衣舞娘，要么是个毫无幽默感的碧池，要么就是丽芙·泰勒。

595
00:26:04.040 --> 00:26:07.060
These are the four categories of woman in this film.
这就是这部电影里女性的四个类别。

596
00:26:07.340 --> 00:26:07.780
Well done.
干得漂亮。

597
00:26:08.000 --> 00:26:08.600
Good breakdown.
剖析得很到位。

598
00:26:08.860 --> 00:26:09.280
Thank you.
谢谢。

599
00:26:09.280 --> 00:26:18.380
I'd also like to say that the fact that Carl is featured so heavily in the beginning of this movie is going to give you the impression that he's going to be some sort of central character,
我还想说，卡尔在这部电影开头戏份如此之重，会给你一种错觉，觉得他会是什么核心角色，

600
00:26:18.380 --> 00:26:22.300
but he's actually going to disappear forever after just a few scenes.
但实际上他在短短几场戏之后就会永远消失。

601
00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:23.640
Yeah, we don't see him again.
是的，我们再也没见到他。

602
00:26:23.800 --> 00:26:29.220
But he does get to name the asteroid because I guess the first person that sees it and clocks it gets to name it.
但他确实给这颗小行星起了名字，因为我猜第一个看到并记录它的人就能给它命名。

603
00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:31.400
He calls NASA and tells them about it.
他打电话给NASA并向他们报告了这件事。

604
00:26:31.480 --> 00:26:34.800
He tells Billy Bob Thornton, I want to name her Dottie after my wife.
他告诉比利·鲍勃·松顿，我想以我妻子的名字把她命名为多蒂。

605
00:26:34.800 --> 00:26:40.940
And then his wife is like, ah, and then he says, because she's a vicious life sucking bitch from which there's no escape.
然后他妻子说，啊，接着他说，因为她是个恶毒的、吸血的、无法逃脱的泼妇。

606
00:26:41.500 --> 00:26:41.680
Yeah.
对。

607
00:26:43.200 --> 00:26:44.300
So there's that.
所以就是这样。

608
00:26:44.580 --> 00:26:44.880
All right.
好了。

609
00:26:44.980 --> 00:26:46.420
Back at command center, everyone.
大家回到指挥中心。

610
00:26:46.740 --> 00:26:47.680
It's DEFCON 3.
这是三级戒备。

611
00:26:48.660 --> 00:26:49.960
Remember the DEFCONs?
还记得防卫等级吗？

612
00:26:50.340 --> 00:26:54.400
Oh, I mean, Billy Bob Thornton is like, you're going to wake up 11,000 people.
哦，我的意思是，比利·鲍勃·松顿就像在说，你们要叫醒11,000人。

613
00:26:54.540 --> 00:26:55.600
Let's get going.
我们开始吧。

614
00:26:56.160 --> 00:26:56.600
Yeah.
是的。

615
00:26:56.600 --> 00:26:59.140
I want to remind you what DEFCON 3 means.
我想提醒大家三级戒备意味着什么。

616
00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:01.280
Oh, Michael Scott would be so excited.
哦，迈克尔·斯科特一定会兴奋极了。

617
00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:01.920
Yes.
没错。

618
00:27:02.060 --> 00:27:07.600
DEFCON 3 means an increase in force readiness above that required for normal readiness.
三级戒备意味着将部队战备状态提高到超过正常战备所需的水平。

619
00:27:07.800 --> 00:27:11.660
It means the Air Force is ready to mobilize in 15 minutes.
这意味着空军准备在15分钟内动员起来。

620
00:27:12.320 --> 00:27:16.440
In America's history, we have been at DEFCON 3 on only a few occasions.
在美国的历史中，我们只有在少数几次情况下处于三级戒备状态。

621
00:27:16.440 --> 00:27:27.340
One, during the Cuban Missile Crisis in 1962, during the 1973 Yom Kippur War, and during the September 11th attack.
一次是1962年的古巴导弹危机，1973年的赎罪日战争，以及911袭击事件。

622
00:27:28.060 --> 00:27:34.280
Incidentally, in movies, we have reached DEFCON 3 in Crimson Tide and Independence Day.
