777
00:33:59.920 --> 00:34:00.120
Right?
对吧？

778
00:34:00.260 --> 00:34:01.440
He called BS on it.
他一眼就看出这是胡扯。

779
00:34:01.620 --> 00:34:07.240
I found an article on mailmagazine.com where they had three drilling engineers fact-check
我在mailmagazine.com上找到了一篇文章，里面有三位钻井工程师对

780
00:34:07.240 --> 00:34:07.980
this movie.
这部电影进行了事实核查。

781
00:34:08.540 --> 00:34:10.780
Let me tell you, they shared my dad's sentiment.
实话告诉你吧，他们的看法跟我爸不谋而合。

782
00:34:11.020 --> 00:34:14.620
One of them said, no way would you fire a gun on a rig.
其中一个人说，在钻井平台上开枪是绝对不可能的。

783
00:34:14.620 --> 00:34:16.580
It would ricochet off of everything.
子弹会在所有东西上到处弹射。

784
00:34:17.300 --> 00:34:17.480
Yeah.
对。

785
00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:20.280
Well, it did do that in the movie.
嗯，电影里确实是这样的。

786
00:34:20.460 --> 00:34:21.640
I mean, there was a lot of ricochet.
我是说，有大量的弹射。

787
00:34:22.020 --> 00:34:23.100
A lot of ricochet.
大量的弹射。

788
00:34:23.300 --> 00:34:25.940
Something ricochets into Ben Affleck's leg.
有什么东西弹射进了本·阿弗莱克的腿里。

789
00:34:26.460 --> 00:34:26.760
Yeah.
对。

790
00:34:27.040 --> 00:34:31.120
And this whole thing is stopped because a helicopter approaches.
而这一切之所以停下来，是因为一架直升机飞过来了。

791
00:34:31.500 --> 00:34:31.820
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

792
00:34:31.920 --> 00:34:34.620
There's a lot of father-daughter tension, a lot of arguing.
这里有很多父女之间的紧张气氛，还有很多争吵。

793
00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:37.300
Grace is saying that it's her life.
格蕾丝说这是她的人生。

794
00:34:37.440 --> 00:34:38.960
She can date who she likes.
她想和谁约会就和谁约会。

795
00:34:39.300 --> 00:34:42.440
Ben Affleck said, you know why we had a helicopter in this movie?
本·阿弗莱克说，你知道为什么我们在这部电影里安排了一架直升机吗？

796
00:34:42.440 --> 00:34:42.960
Why?
为什么？

797
00:34:43.280 --> 00:34:46.820
Because we just wanted to show everyone that we were a big movie that had a ton of money.
因为我们只是想向所有人展示，我们是一部很有钱的大制作电影。

798
00:34:47.120 --> 00:34:47.920
She said it was loud.
她说声音太大了。

799
00:34:48.040 --> 00:34:50.800
You couldn't hear your lines, but they had to have a helicopter.
你根本听不清台词，但他们非得弄一架直升机来。

800
00:34:51.420 --> 00:34:51.560
Yeah.
是啊。

801
00:34:51.740 --> 00:34:56.260
These are the people who are financing this oil drill and they're going to give them a
这些人是这个石油钻探项目的金主，他们准备带他们去

802
00:34:56.260 --> 00:34:56.780
little tour.
参观一下。

803
00:34:56.920 --> 00:35:00.820
Liv Tyler clearly has some role in this business, family business.
丽芙·泰勒显然在这家企业、家族企业里扮演某个角色。

804
00:35:01.100 --> 00:35:02.080
Her dad's rigged.
她爸爸是钻井台工人。

805
00:35:02.140 --> 00:35:04.480
She's like the sort of marketing PR person.
她有点像是市场公关人员。

806
00:35:04.760 --> 00:35:04.810
Yeah.
对。

807
00:35:04.810 --> 00:35:06.500
Like, look, this is what you're spending your money on.
就像是，看吧，这就是你们的钱花在了哪里。

808
00:35:06.600 --> 00:35:06.700
Yeah.
对。

809
00:35:06.800 --> 00:35:08.120
She's now in a nice black dress.
她现在穿着一条漂亮的黑色裙子。

810
00:35:08.120 --> 00:35:09.640
She's in high heels on a rig.
她踩着高跟鞋站在钻井平台上。

811
00:35:09.840 --> 00:35:10.220
Right.
没错。

812
00:35:10.400 --> 00:35:10.740
Right.
没错。

813
00:35:10.880 --> 00:35:11.100
Yeah.
对。

814
00:35:11.240 --> 00:35:13.520
She's showing off everything that's happening.
她正在展示正在发生的这一切。

815
00:35:13.720 --> 00:35:18.700
But we're also going to cut to a lot of problem-solving meetings over at NASA.
但我们也会切换到许多在NASA召开的解决问题的会议。

816
00:35:19.260 --> 00:35:23.600
And they're trying to figure out how are we going to stop this giant meteor?
他们正在想办法，我们该怎么阻止这颗巨大的陨石？

817
00:35:24.740 --> 00:35:30.760
And there's this great scene where they explain, oh, we should just have a nuclear bomb go
有个很棒的场景，他们解释说，哦，我们只要引爆一颗核弹

818
00:35:30.760 --> 00:35:31.000
off.
就行了。

819
00:35:31.120 --> 00:35:32.940
Just shoot a nuclear bomb at it.
直接向它发射一颗核弹。

820
00:35:33.080 --> 00:35:37.500
And the guy is like, no, you have to drill a bomb into the middle.
然后那个人说，不，你必须把炸弹钻进中心。

821
00:35:37.640 --> 00:35:42.740
Because imagine if you held a firecracker in your open hand and it went off, it would
因为想象一下，如果你手里拿一个爆竹然后点燃，它只会

822
00:35:42.740 --> 00:35:43.620
burn your hand.
烫伤你的手。

823
00:35:43.740 --> 00:35:48.360
But if you close your fist around the firecracker and it goes off, it'll blow your hand off.
但如果你把拳头握紧包住爆竹再点燃，它会把你的手炸飞。

824
00:35:48.640 --> 00:35:48.800
Right.
对。

825
00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:50.840
So this is what they have to do.
所以这就是他们必须要做的。

826
00:35:50.980 --> 00:35:56.860
They have to drill a hole and then put a nuclear bomb in the hole of the asteroid.
他们必须钻一个洞，然后把核弹放进小行星的洞里。

827
00:35:57.100 --> 00:35:57.260
Right.
没错。

828
00:35:57.580 --> 00:35:58.940
We're going to cut to the rig now.
我们现在切换到钻井平台。

829
00:35:59.080 --> 00:35:59.760
Something is wrong.
出事了。

830
00:35:59.960 --> 00:36:02.780
They are blowing oil, mud, and gas all over the rig.
石油、泥浆和天然气喷得到钻井平台到处都是。

831
00:36:03.040 --> 00:36:06.060
My dad turned to me and said, that would never happen.
我爸转头对我说，这种事绝不可能发生。

832
00:36:06.060 --> 00:36:07.140
He called bullshit.
他觉得简直是胡扯。

833
00:36:07.320 --> 00:36:09.340
I'm doing such a bad impression of my dad.
我把我爸模仿得太差劲了。

834
00:36:09.680 --> 00:36:11.440
But he would say, never happen.
但他会说，绝对不可能。

835
00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:16.160
According to the drilling engineers that fact-checked this, quote, once said,
根据对这进行核查的钻井工程师们的说法，引述一下，曾经说过，

836
00:36:16.160 --> 00:36:18.940
that's one of the things where the physics doesn't make sense.
这是物理原理说不通的事情之一。

837
00:36:19.140 --> 00:36:23.400
He just goes over there with a big crescent wrench and turns the valve by the standpipe.
他拿着一把大活动扳手走过去，转动了立管旁的阀门。

838
00:36:23.560 --> 00:36:25.120
It makes absolutely no sense.
这完全说不通。

839
00:36:25.380 --> 00:36:26.680
That's not how it works.
根本不是这么运作的。

840
00:36:26.900 --> 00:36:28.840
You secure a well from the rig floor.
你应该从钻井台面控制油井。

841
00:36:28.840 --> 00:36:30.780
You don't secure it from the corner of the derrick.
你不会从井架角落去控制它。

842
00:36:30.980 --> 00:36:34.620
But also, they all just went on and on and said, there's so many safety measures now.
而且，他们喋喋不休地说，现在有很多安全措施。

843
00:36:34.920 --> 00:36:37.520
And it's very slim that anything like that would happen.
发生那种事的几率非常小。

844
00:36:38.160 --> 00:36:45.900
Well, for the plot, I guess this had to happen because it proves that A.J.'s gut was wrong
好吧，为了剧情需要，我想这必须发生，因为它证明了A.J.对二号钻井的直觉

845
00:36:45.900 --> 00:36:47.460
about drill number two.
是错的。

846
00:36:47.780 --> 00:36:47.960
Right.
没错。

847
00:36:48.260 --> 00:36:50.640
Now, you guys, another helicopter is going to come.
好了，各位，另一架直升机要来了。

848
00:36:50.980 --> 00:36:52.560
This time, it's General Montgomery.
这次来的是蒙哥马利将军。

849
00:36:52.900 --> 00:36:53.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

850
00:36:53.580 --> 00:36:55.500
And he's going to say, you've got to come with me.
他会说，你得跟我走。

851
00:36:55.680 --> 00:36:57.400
It's a matter of urgent national security.
这是一个涉及国家安全的紧急问题。

852
00:36:57.880 --> 00:37:00.640
Harry's like, did Crazy Willie put you up to this?
哈里说，是疯子威利让你这么干的吗？

853
00:37:00.840 --> 00:37:04.240
And the general's like, I'm afraid I don't know who Crazy Willie is, sir.
将军说，恐怕我不知道疯子威利是谁，长官。

854
00:37:04.360 --> 00:37:05.060
I'm dead serious.
我是认真的。

855
00:37:06.000 --> 00:37:10.280
And then I think this is when Steve Buscemi's character gets the Creeper Award.
然后我觉得这就是史蒂夫·布西密的角色获得“怪蜀黍奖”的时候。

856
00:37:10.500 --> 00:37:13.460
Yeah, he gets to make a weird underage sex joke.
对，他讲了一个奇怪的未成年人性暗示笑话。

857
00:37:13.640 --> 00:37:13.860
Yeah.
对。

858
00:37:14.140 --> 00:37:17.780
He comes up to Bruce Willis when he sees the helicopter and he says,
他看到直升机时向布鲁斯·威利斯走去，然后他说，

859
00:37:17.900 --> 00:37:20.300
I swear, I didn't know how old she was.
我发誓，我不知道她多大。

860
00:37:20.440 --> 00:37:23.260
This is going to be the beginning of The Creeper Runner.
这将是《怪蜀黍快跑》的开端。

861
00:37:23.420 --> 00:37:25.300
That is Steve Buscemi's character.
那就是史蒂夫·布西密的角色。

862
00:37:25.820 --> 00:37:25.980
Yeah.
对。

863
00:37:26.220 --> 00:37:28.620
And Harry's like, fine, I'll go, but I want to take my daughter
哈里说，好吧，我去，但我想带上我女儿

864
00:37:28.620 --> 00:37:30.860
because he's wanting to get her away from A.J.
因为他想把她从A.J.身边支开。

865
00:37:31.160 --> 00:37:31.500
Yeah.
对。

866
00:37:32.080 --> 00:37:33.880
So they arrive in Houston.
于是他们抵达了休斯顿。

867
00:37:33.880 --> 00:37:36.000
Harry Stamper meets Dan Truman.
哈里·斯坦珀遇到了丹·杜鲁门。

868
00:37:36.500 --> 00:37:40.800
And after a kind of rough hello, they go inside and they bring Harry up to speed.
经过一番不太客气的打招呼后，他们走进室内，向哈里通报了最新情况。

869
00:37:41.120 --> 00:37:45.820
If you are wondering why the entire world is not in a massive panic right now,
如果你在纳闷为什么全世界现在没有陷入巨大恐慌之中，

870
00:37:45.880 --> 00:37:48.300
it's because they're going to tell us.
那是因为他们马上就要向我们通报了。

871
00:37:48.460 --> 00:37:53.000
There are only nine telescopes in the world that can see this asteroid,
世界上只有九架望远镜能看到这颗小行星，

872
00:37:53.000 --> 00:37:54.380
and the U.S.
而美国

873
00:37:54.560 --> 00:37:55.860
controls eight of them.
控制了其中八架。

874
00:37:56.160 --> 00:37:56.320
Yeah.
对。

875
00:37:56.320 --> 00:37:59.520
So they're able to keep this a secret from the whole world,
所以他们能够向全世界隐瞒这件事，

876
00:37:59.760 --> 00:38:04.540
even though most of New York City has been destroyed by a meteor shower.
尽管纽约市的大部分已经被流星雨摧毁。

877
00:38:04.760 --> 00:38:07.840
No one's looking up in the sky except for us.
除了我们，没人抬头看天空。

878
00:38:07.960 --> 00:38:08.420
That's right.
没错。

879
00:38:08.640 --> 00:38:11.220
Bruce Willis has maybe one of my favorite lines in the movie.
布鲁斯·威利斯在电影里有一句我最喜欢的台词。

880
00:38:11.480 --> 00:38:14.120
He says, six billion people on the planet.
他说，地球上有六十亿人。

881
00:38:14.300 --> 00:38:15.580
Why'd you guys call me?
为什么偏偏叫我来？

882
00:38:16.680 --> 00:38:19.020
By the way, in terms of people looking up at the sky,
顺便说一句，就人们抬头看天而言，

883
00:38:19.260 --> 00:38:23.220
I googled how far, because the asteroid's the size of Texas.
我用谷歌搜索了多远，因为这颗小行星有得克萨斯州那么大。

884
00:38:23.480 --> 00:38:28.540
Hypothetically, NASA would know about that decades to centuries before impact, not 18 days.
按理说，美国宇航局在撞击前几十年到几百年就会知道，而不是18天前。

885
00:38:28.900 --> 00:38:32.040
Also, now, since the scene is back in the NASA Space Center,
另外，现在，由于场景回到了美国宇航局太空中心，

886
00:38:32.540 --> 00:38:35.560
Michael Bay had more to say about NASA and its building.
迈克尔·贝对美国宇航局及其建筑有更多看法。

887
00:38:35.840 --> 00:38:36.440
Let's hear it.
我们听听看。

888
00:38:36.880 --> 00:38:39.220
At NASA here, we tried to sexy it up.
在当今的美国宇航局，我们试图把它弄得性感一点。

889
00:38:39.340 --> 00:38:40.080
This is not a building.
这不是一栋大楼。

890
00:38:40.220 --> 00:38:42.720
This is actually, this building sells herbal products.
实际上，这栋大楼是卖草本产品的。

891
00:38:43.260 --> 00:38:47.480
If you saw the real NASA, you just wouldn't trust it as far as you can throw it.
如果你看到真正的美国宇航局，你根本就不会信任它。

892
00:38:47.600 --> 00:38:52.160
It looks very much like an old 60s, 50s kind of school.
它看起来非常像一所50、60年代的老学校。

893
00:38:52.540 --> 00:38:54.960
I was very unimpressed when I went to NASA,
我去美国宇航局时非常失望，

894
00:38:55.540 --> 00:38:58.200
just in terms of just the look and the lack of design.
仅仅是从外观和缺乏设计的角度来看。

895
00:38:58.820 --> 00:39:03.280
But I was also very impressed with just the intelligent people that I met there
但我也对我在那里遇到的一群聪明人

896
00:39:03.280 --> 00:39:04.860
and the systems that they're doing.
以及他们所做系统留下了深刻印象。

897
00:39:04.860 --> 00:39:10.480
So we tried to give NASA a look in our mission control that was stately.
所以我们试图在我们的任务控制中心给美国宇航局一种庄严的外观。

898
00:39:10.660 --> 00:39:14.420
I was creating a NASA that would, what would my perception of NASA be?
我在塑造一个美国宇航局，我心目中的美国宇航局会是什么样？

899
00:39:14.980 --> 00:39:18.900
You guys, I'm telling you, could you not listen to that all day?
伙计们，我告诉你们，你们就不能一整天都不听那个吗？

900
00:39:19.100 --> 00:39:19.320
Yeah.
对。

901
00:39:19.440 --> 00:39:20.800
And look, I'm not kink shaming.
听着，我不是在批判别人的癖好。

902
00:39:20.920 --> 00:39:22.540
I know there's a kink out there for everybody.
我知道什么奇奇怪怪的癖好都有。

903
00:39:22.680 --> 00:39:25.520
This is the first time I've ever seen anybody be horny for NASA.
但我还是头一次见到有人对美国宇航局发春的。

904
00:39:25.960 --> 00:39:27.880
Just as the building itself.
而且是对这栋建筑本身。

905
00:39:29.740 --> 00:39:31.840
Well, not the original building.
好吧，不是原来那栋建筑。

906
00:39:32.020 --> 00:39:32.660
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

907
00:39:33.120 --> 00:39:38.120
So now they're going to take Harry down to this airplane hangar and they're going to show him this drill.
所以现在他们把哈里带到了这个飞机机库里，打算给他看这个钻机。

908
00:39:38.560 --> 00:39:41.040
It's a drill that they stole from him.
这是从他那里偷来的钻机。

909
00:39:41.180 --> 00:39:46.540
His plans that were patented, they stole it from him eight months ago for a Mars project.
他申请了专利的图纸，八个月前被他们偷走用来搞一个火星项目。

910
00:39:46.820 --> 00:39:48.280
And it's not working right.
而且这玩意儿现在出了故障。

911
00:39:48.460 --> 00:39:53.660
And they need him to fix it so that they can take it into space so they can drill into this asteroid.
他们需要他来修好，好带上太空去钻开一颗小行星。

912
00:39:53.660 --> 00:39:59.320
And they have these eight astronauts that they've been training to use the drill.
他们还找了八个宇航员一直在训练怎么用这台钻机。

913
00:39:59.320 --> 00:40:00.800
And they're messing it up.
结果他们把事情搞砸了。

914
00:40:01.080 --> 00:40:08.040
And this leads to Ben Affleck's famous DVD commentary about this scene.
这就引出了本·阿弗莱克关于这场戏的著名DVD评论音轨。

915
00:40:08.260 --> 00:40:08.860
Let's hear it.
我们来听听。

916
00:40:08.860 --> 00:40:14.780
I asked Michael why it was easier to train oil drillers to become astronauts than it was to train
我问迈克尔，为什么教石油钻井工人当宇航员，比教

917
00:40:14.780 --> 00:40:17.920
astronauts to become oil drillers and he told me to shut the f**k up.
宇航员去当石油钻井工人还要容易，结果他让我闭上他妈的嘴。

918
00:40:18.720 --> 00:40:20.220
So that was the end of that talk.
所以那次对话就这么结束了。

919
00:40:20.820 --> 00:40:22.500
He's like, you know, Ben, just shut up, okay?
他当时说，你知道的，本，闭嘴好吗？

920
00:40:22.980 --> 00:40:24.780
You know, this is a real plan, all right?
你知道的，这是个真正的计划，行了吧？

921
00:40:25.620 --> 00:40:29.540
I was like, you mean it's a real plan at NASA to train oil drillers?
我说，你是说美国宇航局真打算训练石油工人？

922
00:40:29.600 --> 00:40:30.740
He was like, just shut your mouth.
他就像是在说，闭上你的臭嘴。

923
00:40:30.740 --> 00:40:32.800
Shut up, Quincy.
闭嘴吧，昆西。

924
00:40:33.120 --> 00:40:36.620
