1520
01:08:02.710 --> 01:08:04.850
And step eight is blow up the asteroid.
第八步是炸毁小行星。

1521
01:08:05.130 --> 01:08:11.110
So we're at step two, which was refuel, and it's already a f***ing s*** show.
所以我们现在正处于第二步，也就是加油，结果已经是一团糟了。

1522
01:08:11.690 --> 01:08:16.010
So now we're going into step three, which is slingshot around the moon.
所以现在我们要进入第三步，也就是绕月飞行借力。

1523
01:08:16.730 --> 01:08:20.570
This is the only step that goes well besides blast-off.
这是除了发射之外唯一顺利的一步。

1524
01:08:20.830 --> 01:08:23.490
I did look up if you can survive at nine Gs.
我确实查过在九个G的重力下人能不能活下来。

1525
01:08:23.630 --> 01:08:23.990
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1526
01:08:24.170 --> 01:08:26.050
I guess you can, but only for a few minutes.
我想是可以的，但只能维持几分钟。

1527
01:08:26.750 --> 01:08:29.490
They are going to be at nine Gs for 11 minutes.
他们要在九个G的重力下承受11分钟。

1528
01:08:30.130 --> 01:08:33.050
One of the astronauts says, this is what we train for.
其中一个宇航员说，这就是我们训练的目的。

1529
01:08:33.310 --> 01:08:34.110
Suck it up.
忍着点吧。

1530
01:08:34.550 --> 01:08:34.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1531
01:08:34.910 --> 01:08:38.670
For Michael Bay, they shot this on a huge gimbal.
对于迈克尔·贝来说，他们是在一个巨大的万向支架上拍摄这一幕的。

1532
01:08:39.110 --> 01:08:45.350
It was an advanced hydraulic platform that was shaking the actors, in his words, quote,
那是一个先进的液压平台，用他自己的话说，会把演员们

1533
01:08:45.690 --> 01:08:49.050
quite violently, forwards, backwards, sideways.
相当剧烈地前后、左右摇晃。

1534
01:08:49.650 --> 01:08:52.090
It was also similar to being in a car accident.
这也类似于遭遇了一场车祸。

1535
01:08:52.390 --> 01:08:52.710
Wow.
哇。

1536
01:08:53.010 --> 01:08:53.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1537
01:08:53.570 --> 01:08:55.870
I mean, they didn't look well.
我是说，他们的脸色可不太好。

1538
01:08:56.010 --> 01:08:56.670
I know.
我知道。

1539
01:08:57.090 --> 01:08:58.710
During this scene.
在这场戏里。

1540
01:08:58.810 --> 01:08:59.990
I thought they looked...
我觉得他们看起来……

1541
01:09:00.550 --> 01:09:02.770
Like they were being shaken quite violently?
就像被相当剧烈地摇晃着一样？

1542
01:09:03.050 --> 01:09:03.310
Yeah.
对。

1543
01:09:03.470 --> 01:09:03.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1544
01:09:03.610 --> 01:09:08.910
I mean, lady, I think about how sometimes on The Office, we would do a scene and they
我是说，老兄，我想起有时候在《办公室》里，我们会拍一场戏，剧本会要求

1545
01:09:08.910 --> 01:09:15.750
would be like, Angela Martin whips her head and gives Kelly a mean look.
安吉拉·马丁猛地转过头给凯莉一个狠厉的眼神。

1546
01:09:15.930 --> 01:09:22.010
And I would have to, like, eight takes in a row, whip my head and give Kelly a mean look.
然后我不得不连续拍八条，猛地转过头去给凯莉一个狠厉的眼神。

1547
01:09:22.230 --> 01:09:23.570
And I'd whip my head back.
然后我再把头甩回来。

1548
01:09:23.890 --> 01:09:25.190
And I'd be sore.
搞得我浑身酸痛。

1549
01:09:25.830 --> 01:09:26.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1550
01:09:26.490 --> 01:09:29.750
How do you feel after you're in a gimbal being shaken quite violently?
你在一个被相当剧烈摇晃的万向支架里待过之后感觉怎么样？

1551
01:09:30.690 --> 01:09:31.410
I don't know.
我不知道。

1552
01:09:31.530 --> 01:09:32.090
I don't know.
我不知道。

1553
01:09:32.090 --> 01:09:33.590
But you have new teeth, so.
但你有了新牙齿，所以嘛。

1554
01:09:34.030 --> 01:09:35.470
I guess you have that.
我想你至少还有这个。

1555
01:09:35.650 --> 01:09:36.310
You've got that.
你至少有这个。

1556
01:09:36.770 --> 01:09:37.510
Step four.
第四步。

1557
01:09:37.690 --> 01:09:38.670
We're at step four now.
我们现在进行到第四步了。

1558
01:09:39.090 --> 01:09:40.950
They need to land on the asteroid.
他们需要在小行星上着陆。

1559
01:09:41.210 --> 01:09:42.070
Here is what I wrote.
这是我写的。

1560
01:09:42.330 --> 01:09:42.710
How?
怎么会？

1561
01:09:43.110 --> 01:09:43.990
Literally how?
简直怎么可能？

1562
01:09:44.450 --> 01:09:48.650
Because little asteroids are kind of falling off the big asteroid.
因为小块的小行星正在从大块的小行星上掉落。

1563
01:09:49.030 --> 01:09:50.630
They're flying through space.
它们在太空中飞驰。

1564
01:09:50.630 --> 01:09:56.650
You're, like, flying through all of this debris to land on a moving object that's all jaggedy.
你们就像是在这些碎片中穿梭，去降落在一个全都是锯齿状的移动物体上。

1565
01:09:56.650 --> 01:09:59.830
I wondered, can space shuttles really fly like this?
我在想，太空梭真的能这样飞吗？

1566
01:09:59.830 --> 01:10:03.530
Because they're flying these two space shuttles like they're the Millennium Falcon.
因为他们开这两艘太空梭的样子就像是在开千年隼号。

1567
01:10:04.210 --> 01:10:05.170
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1568
01:10:05.310 --> 01:10:06.770
The answer is no.
答案是不能。

1569
01:10:07.430 --> 01:10:09.730
Real space shuttles are gliders.
真正的太空梭是滑翔机。

1570
01:10:10.110 --> 01:10:13.410
They cannot take off or maneuver around an asteroid.
它们无法在小行星周围起飞或机动飞行。

1571
01:10:13.630 --> 01:10:14.830
They don't fly like that.
它们不是那样飞的。

1572
01:10:14.830 --> 01:10:19.590
But that's why we learned early in the movie that these are special.
但这就是为什么我们在电影开头就得知这些是特殊的。

1573
01:10:20.370 --> 01:10:25.150
They've got special reinforcements and they can fly like all this shit.
它们有特殊的加固装置，可以这样胡乱飞行。

1574
01:10:25.490 --> 01:10:25.670
Yeah.
对。

1575
01:10:25.930 --> 01:10:29.590
But guess what happens as they're trying to land on the asteroid?
但你猜当他们试图在小行星上着陆时会发生什么？

1576
01:10:29.930 --> 01:10:32.890
Well, they lose the Independence aircraft.
嗯，他们失去了独立号飞船。

1577
01:10:33.230 --> 01:10:34.030
That one's a goner.
那一艘完蛋了。

1578
01:10:34.230 --> 01:10:35.270
Can I just say something?
我能说句话吗？

1579
01:10:35.530 --> 01:10:40.690
Immediately at the beginning of this movie when they told me that they were going to be dividing into two shuttles.
就在这部电影刚开始时，当他们告诉我他们要分成两艘太空梭时。

1580
01:10:40.690 --> 01:10:41.010
Yeah.
对。

1581
01:10:41.310 --> 01:10:41.730
You know.
你知道的。

1582
01:10:41.910 --> 01:10:44.890
I'm thinking to myself, dear God, let me be on the one.
我心里想，天哪，让我登上那一艘吧。

1583
01:10:45.050 --> 01:10:45.930
With Bruce Willis?
跟布鲁斯·威利斯一起的那艘？

1584
01:10:45.990 --> 01:10:46.170
Yeah.
对。

1585
01:10:46.250 --> 01:10:46.650
Yeah, me too.
对，我也是。

1586
01:10:46.650 --> 01:10:48.770
Because we know the other one is going down.
因为我们知道另一艘要坠毁。

1587
01:10:48.930 --> 01:10:50.110
But AJ's on the other one.
但AJ在另一艘上。

1588
01:10:50.250 --> 01:10:51.290
Ben Affleck's on the other one.
本·阿弗莱克在另一艘上。

1589
01:10:51.370 --> 01:10:51.830
He is.
确实在。

1590
01:10:51.970 --> 01:10:52.910
And it goes down.
然后它坠毁了。

1591
01:10:53.170 --> 01:10:53.470
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1592
01:10:53.870 --> 01:11:01.070
One of my favorite moments is that as the asteroid hits the Independence, we cut back to NASA.
我最喜欢的时刻之一就是，当小行星撞击独立号时，镜头切回了NASA。

1593
01:11:01.450 --> 01:11:05.150
And you see Billy Bob Thornton's coffee mug drop.
然后你看到比利·鲍伯·松顿的咖啡杯掉了下来。

1594
01:11:05.250 --> 01:11:08.130
And it hits the side of the table and it breaks.
它撞到了桌子边然后碎了。

1595
01:11:08.530 --> 01:11:09.930
Oh, I miss that.
哦，我错过那个了。

1596
01:11:09.930 --> 01:11:12.130
So there's tragedy all around, okay?
所以到处都是悲剧，好吗？

1597
01:11:12.290 --> 01:11:15.710
Even back at NASA, things are breaking.
甚至连NASA总部，东西都在破碎。

1598
01:11:15.950 --> 01:11:16.850
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1599
01:11:16.990 --> 01:11:18.770
I'm surprised it doesn't burst into flames.
我很惊讶它竟然没有直接起火爆炸。

1600
01:11:19.570 --> 01:11:20.130
Exactly.
正是如此。

1601
01:11:21.030 --> 01:11:24.390
Like that it didn't like spill onto the control center.
就像它没有溅到控制中心一样。

1602
01:11:24.870 --> 01:11:25.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1603
01:11:25.690 --> 01:11:26.090
Same.
我也是。

1604
01:11:26.430 --> 01:11:26.710
All right.
好吧。

1605
01:11:26.790 --> 01:11:29.770
I want you to know what I wrote down during this scene.
我想让你知道我在这场戏里写下了什么。

1606
01:11:29.950 --> 01:11:31.130
Here's what I wrote.
这是我写的。

1607
01:11:31.450 --> 01:11:35.970
How did they imagine it was ever possible to land on this asteroid?
他们怎么会觉得登陆这颗小行星是有可能的？

1608
01:11:36.210 --> 01:11:36.870
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

1609
01:11:37.050 --> 01:11:37.830
They're hit again.
他们又挨炸了。

1610
01:11:37.830 --> 01:11:40.610
Again, now astronauts are being sucked out of the windows.
紧接着，宇航员们被吸出了窗外。

1611
01:11:40.610 --> 01:11:42.510
But wait, are some of them escaping?
等等，他们中有人逃生了吗？

1612
01:11:42.850 --> 01:11:43.570
Oh, shit.
哦，靠。

1613
01:11:43.610 --> 01:11:45.370
I think Owen Wilson just died.
我觉得欧文·威尔逊刚死。

1614
01:11:46.030 --> 01:11:50.150
Bruce Willis' ship is now getting hit with debris from the other shuttles.
布鲁斯·威利斯的飞船现在被其他航天飞机洒下的碎片击中了。

1615
01:11:50.350 --> 01:11:52.610
And Bruce Willis says, quote, what is that?
然后布鲁斯·威利斯说，原话是，那是什么？

1616
01:11:52.770 --> 01:11:53.830
Is that the Independence?
那是“独立号”吗？

1617
01:11:53.830 --> 01:11:58.390
And right after that, an astronaut is hurled into his window.
就在那之后，一名宇航员被撞向他的窗户。

1618
01:11:58.630 --> 01:11:58.970
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1619
01:11:59.410 --> 01:11:59.690
Yeah.
是啊。

1620
01:11:59.890 --> 01:12:04.510
So, yes, the Independence has crashed onto the surface of the asteroid.
所以，是的，“独立号”已经坠毁在小行星表面了。

1621
01:12:04.790 --> 01:12:07.330
But I think Ben Affleck is still alive.
但我认为本·阿弗莱克还活着。

1622
01:12:07.330 --> 01:12:09.170
Well, we find out.
好吧，我们拭目以待。

1623
01:12:09.350 --> 01:12:16.150
We find out that Ben Affleck, so AJ, Bear, and the Russian, they made it somehow.
我们发现本·阿弗莱克，也就是说AJ、贝尔和那个俄罗斯人，不知怎么的活了下来。

1624
01:12:16.710 --> 01:12:19.030
But back at Houston, it's assumed they're all dead.
但在休斯顿总部，大家以为他们全死了。

1625
01:12:19.170 --> 01:12:19.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1626
01:12:19.450 --> 01:12:20.310
Nobody knows this.
没人知道这一点。

1627
01:12:20.430 --> 01:12:23.790
There's some montages back in Houston of, like, worried, sad people.
休斯顿那边有一些剪辑镜头，都是些焦虑、悲伤的人。

1628
01:12:24.130 --> 01:12:24.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1629
01:12:24.370 --> 01:12:31.670
But now, Bruce Willis' team, they get out that big buggy thing, you know, the armadillo.
但现在，布鲁斯·威利斯的团队开出了那个大号越野车，你知道的，那个“犰狳号”。

1630
01:12:31.910 --> 01:12:32.410
They land.
他们着陆了。

1631
01:12:32.690 --> 01:12:32.740
They land.
他们着陆了。

1632
01:12:32.740 --> 01:12:34.930
But they overshot their landing field, lady.
但大姐，他们飞过着陆区了。

1633
01:12:35.230 --> 01:12:35.470
Oh.
哦。

1634
01:12:35.470 --> 01:12:36.370
They overshot it.
他们飞过头了。

1635
01:12:36.470 --> 01:12:38.090
I was like, there's a landing field?
当时我就想，这里还有着陆区？

1636
01:12:38.090 --> 01:12:39.470
By 26 miles.
偏离了26英里。

1637
01:12:39.830 --> 01:12:41.050
I mean, my God.
我的天呐。

1638
01:12:41.370 --> 01:12:43.530
They didn't even know what the asteroid looked like up close.
他们甚至连小行星近看是什么样都不知道。

1639
01:12:43.530 --> 01:12:45.090
How do they know there's a landing field?
他们怎么知道那里有个着陆区？

1640
01:12:45.150 --> 01:12:45.870
I don't know.
我不知道。

1641
01:12:45.870 --> 01:12:50.750
But also, now their communication system is not going well.
而且现在他们的通讯系统也不太妙。

1642
01:12:51.010 --> 01:12:56.910
And they've also landed on mostly iron rock, which, as we all know, at this point, is horrible
他们还降落在了主要是铁质的岩石上，正如我们大家现在所知道的，这太糟糕了

1643
01:12:56.910 --> 01:12:57.650
to drill in.
根本没法钻孔。

1644
01:12:57.750 --> 01:12:58.530
Iron rock.
铁质岩石。

1645
01:12:58.690 --> 01:12:59.870
Can't drill through it.
根本钻不透。

1646
01:13:00.010 --> 01:13:00.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1647
01:13:00.550 --> 01:13:04.170
So now we're going to start on step five, which is drilling the hole.
所以现在我们要开始第五步，也就是钻孔。

1648
01:13:04.350 --> 01:13:05.530
And they have eight hours.
他们有八个小时。

1649
01:13:05.870 --> 01:13:06.550
Eight hours.
八个小时。

1650
01:13:06.710 --> 01:13:07.870
They have to get 800 feet.
他们必须钻到800英尺深。

1651
01:13:08.130 --> 01:13:08.530
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1652
01:13:08.630 --> 01:13:11.910
They break their first drill bit in 10 feet.
他们钻头才钻了10英尺就断了。

1653
01:13:12.230 --> 01:13:12.570
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1654
01:13:13.030 --> 01:13:13.630
They do.
确实如此。

1655
01:13:13.630 --> 01:13:19.470
Here was another question that I had, which was, how are they walking on the asteroid?
我还有另一个问题，那就是他们在小行星上是怎么走路的？

1656
01:13:20.170 --> 01:13:25.090
How is this rover thing staying stuck to the surface of the asteroid?
这个漫游车是怎么黏在小行星表面的？

1657
01:13:25.190 --> 01:13:26.670
Why is it not floating away?
为什么它没有飘走？

1658
01:13:26.810 --> 01:13:29.330
Why is there gravity on the asteroid?
为什么小行星上有重力？

1659
01:13:30.170 --> 01:13:31.150
I looked it up.
我查了一下。

1660
01:13:31.230 --> 01:13:33.150
There would not be gravity on the asteroid.
小行星上本不该有重力。

1661
01:13:33.770 --> 01:13:38.610
Again, early in the movie, we have this little moment where they explain that their suits,
再说一遍，电影刚开始不久，有这么一个小片段，他们解释说他们的宇航服，

1662
01:13:38.630 --> 01:13:40.670
remember when they're not paying attention to the woman?
还记得他们当时没听那个女人讲话吗？

1663
01:13:40.670 --> 01:13:46.070
She's explaining that their suits have special little thrusters that will keep them stuck
她在解释说他们的宇航服带有特殊的微型推进器，能让他们

1664
01:13:46.070 --> 01:13:46.990
to the asteroid.
黏在小行星上。

1665
01:13:47.150 --> 01:13:48.770
But no one is using the thrusters.
但根本没人用这些推进器。

1666
01:13:49.070 --> 01:13:49.730
No one's using them.
根本没人用。

1667
01:13:50.050 --> 01:13:50.100
No one.
一个人都没有。

1668
01:13:50.170 --> 01:13:52.430
You never see evidence of these thrusters.
你根本看不到任何使用这些推进器的迹象。

1669
01:13:52.670 --> 01:13:52.910
Yeah.
对啊。

1670
01:13:53.090 --> 01:13:54.290
It's very strange.
这太奇怪了。

1671
01:13:55.510 --> 01:14:01.950
Neil deGrasse Tyson said that until the release of the 2022 film Moonfall, Armageddon was the
尼尔·德格拉斯·泰森曾说过，在2022年电影《月球陨落》上映之前，《绝世天劫》是

1672
01:14:01.950 --> 01:14:06.310
movie which violated more laws of physics per minute than any other movie ever.
史上每分钟违反物理定律最多的电影。

1673
01:14:06.310 --> 01:14:12.130
And NASA shows this film during their management training program, and new managers are given
而且美国宇航局在他们的管理培训项目里会放映这部电影，新管理者们的任务

1674
01:14:12.130 --> 01:14:15.290
the task of trying to spot as many errors as possible.
就是尽可能多地找出其中的错误。

1675
01:14:15.610 --> 01:14:19.430
So far, they've spotted at least 168.
到目前为止，他们已经找出了至少168个。

1676
01:14:20.230 --> 01:14:27.530
So NASA uses this movie the way Human Resources uses an episode of The Office of how not to behave
所以美国宇航局利用这部电影的方式，就像人力资源部门拿《办公室》的一集来当

1677
01:14:27.530 --> 01:14:28.250
at the office.
办公室反面教材一样。

1678
01:14:28.630 --> 01:14:29.110
Yes.
没错。

1679
01:14:29.330 --> 01:14:34.810
And this is, can you tell me everything that's wrong from a scientific point of view?
这就好比，你能从科学的角度告诉我哪里不对劲吗？

